    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70">

                <pb facs="0153" n="133" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg133"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">357.AD/6–2550: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Korea</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Muccio</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-06-25T20:00:00+10:00">June 25, 1950, 8
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 25—7:38 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>938. Embtel 933, June 25.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d70-f1"/>
                    UNCOK chairman Liu informs us that at meeting
                    today UNCOK resolved send report to Secretary
                    General <pb facs="0154" n="134" xml:id="pg134"/> UN setting forth all facts re
                    hostilities gathered to date.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d70-f2"/> Message will
                    further state UNCOK regards situation as
                    serious and one which may assume status of full-fledged war. Message will ask
                    Secretary General to consider inviting attention of SC to matter. Liu stressed
                    message will only ask Secretary General consider possibility of bringing matter
                    to SC. Liu went on to say that if situation “deteriorates tomorrow” UNCOK will probably send further message
                    definitely requesting Secretary General to put matter before SC.</p>
                <p>Liu further stated UNCOK decided he should go
                    on air at 9 o’clock Seoul time on GHT and broadcast one or two minute appeal for
                    both sides to cease-fire.</p>
                <p>Theme will be Koreans should not fight Koreans. Broadcast will include offer to
                    mediate with view to peaceful settlement.</p>
                <p>Text of broadcast will be telegraphed when available.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d70-f3"/> Suggest USUN endeavor
                    obtain copy of UNCOK message to Secretary
                    General referred to above.</p>
                <p>Repeated info CINCFE Tokyo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Muccio</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d70-f1" n="1" xml:id="d70-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed, but see footnote 1 to telegram 935, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d70-f2" n="2" xml:id="d70-f2-content">
                <p>
                    UNCOK’s report to the Secretary General was
                    distributed as U.N. document S/1496. For further information on this document,
                    see the memorandum of conversation by Mr. Noyes, June 25, <ref target="#pg144"
                        >p. 144</ref>, and telegram 541, June 26, from New York, <ref
                        target="#pg171">p. 171</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d70-f3" n="3" xml:id="d70-f3-content">
                <p>See U.N. document A/1350, <ref target="#pg3">p. 3</ref>, and U.N. document
                    A/AC.26/SR.32.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
